# Frontend async UX

While a trip has an in-flight plan or crew job:

- Treat `planning_day_index` / `crew_job_kind` (or matching mutation `isPending`) as locked.
- Disable conflicting actions (e.g. suggest-place during day planning) — do not rely on the API 409 alone.
- On async failure, refresh from `GET /trips/:id` so stale claim fields from `onAsyncStarted` do not stick in local state.
- Do not auto-start `plan-next-day` when `status === "failed"`; user must click Plan next day.
- Prefer surfacing `planning_error` / mapped API codes over generic timeouts when the server already failed.
